Fix the ownership authorization module raising an authorization error for every non-admin save/modify, including creating new objects, instead of correctly checking ownership against the object itself. Removing, copying, and modifying templates, menus, network interfaces, and the group item types also no longer crash with the same error, and copying an object now correctly requires ownership instead of always being denied for non-admins. Also close a name-collision gap where a new object could be used to bypass the real owner of an already-existing, differently-owned object of the same name.
